  "term": "Agraphia",
  "definition": "Agraphia is a loss or reduction in the ability to write letters, syllables, words, or phrases. It is usually linked to injury in a specific area of the brain, though it can sometimes be related to emotional factors, and it often occurs along with aphasia rather than by itself.",
